@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' Destination diagram — prose from internal/workspace/{mount,workspace,discover}.go and
' cmd/proveo/main.go's mount + env-forwarding blocks lands here (batches 3 and 6).
' Escaping symlinks have their own diagram: mount-symlink-escape.puml.
title Mount model — two layouts, one scope resolver, secrets decided by egress

' covers: internal/workspace/mount.go

node "Scope resolution" as SCOPE <<host>> {
  component "workspace.Resolve(dir)\nScope{Root, Prefix, IsRepo}" as RES <<app>>
  component "DiscoverProjects(root)\npnpm · npm/yarn · convention globs" as DISC <<app>>
  component "scope picker\n--scope, else a TTY menu" as PICK <<app>>
}

node "MountSpec.Plan() — manifest workspace model" as PLAN <<host>> {
  component "layout: app\n/app + /app/output" as IO <<app>>
  component "layout: app\nagent edits in place at /app" as APP <<app>>
  component "monorepo subdir scope\n/app/<rel> + /app/.git + rootFiles" as SUB <<app>>
  component "envMounts · maskEnvMounts\nescapingEnvFile" as ENV <<app>>
}

database "Host checkout\nmode ro|rw · gitMode ro|rw" as HOST <<db>>
component "runner.Mount list\nhost:container[:ro]" as MOUNTS <<app>>
component "Secrets readable inside the agent\n.env left in the mounted tree" as LEAK <<error>>

RES ARROW_MAIN PICK : repo root vs subdir
DISC ARROW_MAIN PICK
PICK ARROW_MAIN PLAN : InputDir · RepoRoot
PLAN ARROW_MAIN IO
PLAN ARROW_MAIN APP
APP ARROW_OPTIONAL SUB : InputDir under RepoRoot
IO ARROW_MAIN ENV
APP ARROW_MAIN ENV
SUB ARROW_MAIN ENV
HOST ARROW_MAIN MOUNTS
ENV ARROW_MAIN MOUNTS
ENV ARROW_ERROR LEAK : what isolating egress exists to prevent

note left of RES
  **Resolution starts from the repository root, not from the directory the
  command was invoked in.** ""--input"" (or the cwd) only says where to start
  looking; the root is what carries full git and workspace context, so once
  ""workspace\.Resolve"" reports a repo everything downstream hangs off the
  root instead of the entry point — the default ""reports/"" output dir,
  project discovery for the picker, and the tree the app layout
  mounts read-only.
end note

note right of PICK
  **The picker opens only when every condition holds: no explicit ""--scope"",
  a repo, a TTY, and not a print-only run.** An explicit ""--scope"" is the
  answer and needs no question; a run that only prints its argv has nothing
  to ask about.

  ""PROVEO_WIZARD=off"" suppresses it — deliberately the same switch as the
  missing-env wizard, so one variable silences every prompt rather than one
  per prompt. A PTY-driven, non-interactive caller — the agent E2E suite, CI
  — would otherwise block forever on a keypress nobody is there to press:
  a PTY //passes// the TTY check, so the TTY check alone is not enough.

  **Two pickers behind one call.** On a real TTY ""pickProject"" shows an
  fzf-style arrow-key + type-to-filter finder; when its reader is a pipe or
  a test's ""strings\.Reader"" it falls back to a numbered prompt driven by
  that reader. The fallback is not a downgrade for looks: the fuzzy finder
  reads ""/dev/tty"" directly and so escapes any injected reader, which is
  exactly what would make tests and CI non-hermetic.

  **Anything unresolved means the repo root.** Entry 0 is ""<repo root>"", and
  Esc/Ctrl-C (""ErrAbort""), a finder failure, and any invalid or empty
  numbered input all resolve to the empty scope — the whole repo, never a
  half-chosen subdirectory. Whether stdin counts as a terminal at all is one
  shared ioctl check, described in
  ""_spec/internal/choiceui/choice-prompt-render\.puml"".
end note

note bottom of ENV
  **Model and UI preferences are forwarded by value, never read from a file
  inside the container.** They are the non-secret half of the environment —
  the shared baseline plus whatever this harness declares in ""config:"" — and
  each entrypoint bridges them into its own tool-specific variable
  (""OPENCODE_MODEL"", ""CECLI_MODEL"", ""ANTHROPIC_MODEL"", …).

  They //must// arrive as env because the file they would otherwise be read
  from is not there to read: ""\.env"" is masked on the proxy and firewall
  tiers, and the app layout does not mount it at all.

  **""--local-model"" overrides them by construction, not by a conditional.**
  Its ""-e"" pairs land in ""plan\.AgentArgs"", which docker applies //after//
  ""Env"", so the later assignment is the one the agent process sees.

  Secrets do not travel this path: they are declared in ""env:"" and go through
  the broker (""_spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary\.puml"").
end note
note right of ENV
  **Masking is recursive and uses ""/dev/null"", not omission.** Every dotenv
  secrets file under the mounted tree is shadowed, so a hostile or injected
  agent cannot read a real credential off disk — the structural complement
  to the broker's header-strip and the egress DLP. Templates
  (""\.env\.example"" / ""\.sample"" / ""\.template"" / ""\.dist"") stay readable,
  because agents legitimately consult them.

  The walk prunes ""\.git"" and ""node_modules"" only — deliberately narrower
  than the shared prune set, since a secrets file inside ""dist/"" still has
  to be masked. It does not follow symlinks, so there are no loops and a
  symlinked ""\.env"" is still masked at its container path.

  **Two mounted sets are deliberately not walked**: the hoisted repo-root
  files are a fixed non-secret allowlist, and the config dir is a
  tool-config directory — neither is a conventional secrets location, and
  walking them would add cost for no coverage.

  For broker ingestion the host-side ""\.env"" is resolved through symlinks
  on the host, following the invocation dir → scope → repo-root order the
  Bash lifecycle used, so a project that symlinks its env file still feeds
  the broker.
end note

note right of SUB
  The hoisted root files are a superset across harnesses, each mounted only
  when it exists at the root **and** is absent from the scope dir — so the
  union is safe: a harness never sees a file its repo does not have, and a
  scope that ships its own ""package\.json"" keeps it.
end note

note bottom of SUB
  **Root dependency isolation via plain copy overlay.** Host ""node_modules""
  is plain-copied to a temp dir and that copy is mounted rw at
  ""/app/node_modules"", overlay-hiding the host tree inside the workspace
  mount — both whole-repo ""/app"" and subdir ""/app/<rel>"" scopes. Host and
  container stay independent; when OS/arch matches the copy reuses the host
  tree, otherwise the container can reinstall without rewriting the host.
  Controlled by ""PROVEO_MOUNT_ROOT_DEPS"" (0 omits the copy).
end note


note as SBX_PARENT
  **sbx mirrors host paths, so a narrow mount can synthesize a lie.**
  Docker remaps container paths freely, so mounting a linked worktree's
  ""<repo>/.git"" alone costs nothing. sbx cannot remap: every workspace lands at
  its own host path, so the ""<repo>"" PARENT must be conjured inside the VM, and
  the runtime creates it root-owned and empty.

  That stub then impersonates the operator's repo root. Measured: host ""<repo>""
  stayed ""pluvo:staff"" throughout while the in-sandbox path read ""root:root 755""
  and refused every write — so tools resolving the MAIN repository directory
  (nx keeps its shared task DB there) failed on a path the operator knew was
  theirs, and the diagnosis went hunting a root-promotion that never happened.

  ""workspaceBinds"" therefore rewrites that one bind to the parent for sbx, and
  only for sbx. The path becomes a real uid-mapped bind — ""claude:claude"", writable
  from host and agent alike — with ""git rev-parse"" still resolving the worktree
  and its common dir. Read-only git keeps its posture: the rewrite moves the
  path, never the ""ro"" flag.
end note

@enduml
